course: dictionary
lesson: 14361
title: Oozing and showing a lot
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word oozing has more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one fits. «Sticky, oozing honey dripped slowly off the spoon.» Honey is a thick liquid, so oozing means slowly flowing out of something.
explain: Oozing can also mean showing a lot of a quality. «Mia walked into the room oozing confidence.» Nobody is leaking anything here. Mia looks very sure of herself, so oozing means showing plenty of it.
explain: When oozing is used as an adjective, it describes something that is slowly leaking. «The cut was oozing, so Mum cleaned it.» The cut is the thing that is leaking. Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Oozing means slowly flowing or leaking out of something, like thick liquid.
fact: Oozing with a quality means showing a lot of it, as in «oozing confidence» or «oozing charm».
fact: An oozing cut keeps leaking, so clean it well and see a doctor if it does not stop.
fact: Ooze is a verb: ooze, oozes, oozed, oozing.
fact: Look at the words around oozing to work out which meaning fits.
exercise: «Sticky, oozing honey dripped slowly off the spoon.» What does oozing mean here? | Dry and crumbly | *Slowly flowing out, like a thick liquid | Frozen solid | Very fast and loud
exercise: «Mia walked into the room oozing confidence.» What does oozing show about Mia? | She felt very cold | She was leaking something | *She showed lots of confidence | She was lost and afraid
exercise: Find and copy the word from this sentence that means flowing out slowly: «The lava was oozing slowly down the side of the volcano.» | volcano | side | lava | *oozing
test: «The cut was oozing, so Mum cleaned it and put on a plaster.» What does oozing describe in this sentence? | A bright and sunny sky | *A cut that is slowly leaking | A room full of people | A plaster that is brand new
test: Which sentence uses oozing to mean showing a lot of something? | *«He walked onto the stage oozing charm.» | «The mud was oozing into the boots.» | «The old tap was oozing all night.» | «The lava was oozing down the hill.»
exam: Which word means slowly leaking out, like thick jam? | Sparkling | Glowing | Barking | *Oozing
